# Apache Web Server Security Audit

## Overview  
In this lab, I assumed the role of a **Security Engineer** tasked with validating that security requirements were implemented correctly on a newly built Apache web server.  
The goal was to ensure the server adhered to baseline security best practices before moving into production.  

---

## Lab Objectives  
- Verify Apache version is up to date.  
- Confirm directory listing is disabled.  
- Ensure Apache does not reveal its version in HTTP headers.  
- Test redirection from HTTP → HTTPS.  
- Validate SSL certificate configuration.  

